&efg=eyJ2ZW5jb2RlX3RhZyI6IkNMSVBTLnhwaWRzLjEwODAuc2RyLnZpZGVvX2RlZmF1bHRfY292ZXJfZnJhbWUuQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=ZS8rqkHfFGsQ7kNvwFqhSfG&_nc_oc=AdpugesHa_S3hl01dEtiN1djaPmZFPCm8-8kxzuq_qLqt9IjrtPO4O41Bjnqc4wq5KjCX0_cuX0tTFR1PENSPzZg&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=instagram.fblr2-2.fna&_nc_gid=-YvLB4vwHtLjuIpjXfyUgQ&_nc_ss=70689&oh=00_AQSyeEqyHZGn0mbA1jdb32CQtMjy8f9kSsGGu8fsxZrJrQ&oe=6AF80200", "width": 1080, "height": 1920, "id": "12", "resolution": "1080x1920"}], "comments": [{"author": "jus_brutal", "author_id": "2016458007", "id": "18112821944266443", "text": "✌🏻", "timestamp": 1794186450, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "rakesh_pratap_singh_chauhan", "author_id": "1754237349", "id": "18129014606305128", "text": "Slight corrections. Kumbhaka technically denotes deliberate or intentional breath retention. The spontaneous or natural cessation of breath that arises effortlessly without manipulation is known as Kevala Kumbhaka or Madhya Dasha. Also, Prana is the upward or inward moving air while Apana is the downward or outward-moving air.", "timestamp": 1793894285, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "kbpathak18", "author_id": "26644221845", "id": "18118195946597326", "text": "Inward breath is Prana and outward is apana... isn't it?", "timestamp": 1793865329, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "sundar_818", "author_id": "59337096953", "id": "18112616849621935", "text": "Thanks 🙏", "timestamp": 1793668886, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "medswebdev", "author_id": "46873630037", "id": "18122617352473496", "text": "Is there any old book where this all has written please suggest that book to me", "timestamp": 1793639471, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "veeraswamyamara", "author_id": "6794529556", "id": "18171685798490253", "text": "A luminous treatise of non-dualist esotericism, the Vijnana Bhairava Tantra stands as an apogee of Pratyabhijñā epistemology—a radical manual of interior phenomenology where the corporeal dissolves into the unconditioned absolute. Rather than prescribing orthodox propitiation or exoteric dogmatism, the text unfolds as a dialogue between Bhairava and Bhairavi, articulating 112 dharanas: granular, phenomenological incursions designed to arrest the compulsive gyration of the citta and puncture mundane reality.\n​What distinguishes this text is its uncompromising psychological acuity. It bypasses the arid dialectics of dry scholasticism, deploying instead a pragmatic, often harrowing praxis. Through radical somatic awareness—attending to the interstitial void between inhalation and exhalation, the sudden dissolution of fear, or the acoustic resonance of raw phonemes—the aspirant is goaded past the dualistic strictures of subject and object. It is a text that does not merely invite contemplation; it demands an ontological liquidation, dissolving the illusory ego into the boundless, self-luminous expanse of cit-prakasa.", "timestamp": 1793633046, "like_count": 2}, {"author": "g.devi_prasad", "author_id": "72831789531", "id": "18288537292290018", "text": "Great explanation ❤️", "timestamp": 1793621605, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "shrivastava2667", "author_id": "6052298627", "id": "18127186966920802", "text": "Why is the creator unnecessarily being so sophisticated adding a after every Sanskrit word", "timestamp": 1793607968, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "shiv_shakti_333777", "author_id": "63709504828", "id": "18200779465388493", "text": "🙌", "timestamp": 1793570977, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "being_ecstatic", "author_id": "4306987139", "id": "18127793434672227", "text": "❤️", "timestamp": 1793561943, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "bira_lp", "author_id": "68928200300", "id": "18342369916277726", "text": "Same thing....", "timestamp": 1793560254, "like_count": 1}, {"author": "__jeswin_____", "author_id": "7456867693", "id": "18022947365939739", "text": "❤️", "timestamp": 1793557836, "like_count": 1}], "webpage_url": "https://www.instagram.com/p/DfLz4E6o6XT/", "webpage_url_basename": "DfLz4E6o6XT", "webpage_url_domain": "instagram.com", "extract